                <pb facs="0473" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00/285 Suppl.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-13T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Refer to my September 12, 2 p.m. According to press reports military junta
                    has accepted Alessandri’s resignation. It is reported from Buenos Aires that
                    Alessandri has made statement that he was banished and that there is no
                    constitutional government in Chile.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to avoid any formal relations with the new regime until the
                    situation clears up, but do not make your course conspicuous. Should a situation
                    arise where it would be impossible to remain noncommittal telegraph Department
                    at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
